Subject: [PATCH] C13's follow-ups, patch 2 (cld-advisor, at main's word in
 M23, a finding on the gate): A WAIVER OF THE REVIEW'S BLOCK COVERS ONLY THE
 WINDOW IT WAS GRANTED IN: THE GATE READS THE ANCHOR IT WAS GRANTED UNDER, AND
 IT EXPIRES WHEN A LATER ANCHOR IS WRITTEN

Main's M23: a waiver is read by its date, and the next window's anchor can carry the same date, so a waiver granted for
one review also covers the next window. Let a waiver name the anchor of the window it was granted in, and expire when a
later anchor is written.

- scripts/gates/gates.py: review_waiver_covers takes the last anchor and a reader of the anchor each line was granted
  under. A line covers only if that anchor is the last one: the anchor the line names ("..., in the window after anchor
  <commit>: ..."), or else the one git's history gives, REVIEWS.md read at the first commit whose waiver file holds the
  line. Where neither is known, the date rule of Review 75 is read, as before. Two helpers: review_anchor and
  waiver_granted_under. The gate passes both.
- No waiver line is edited. The three on record read, from history: the waiver of 2026-11-05 under 41420ae14, of
  2026-11-11 under 38d2a36dc, of 2026-11-13 under c40446392 (Review 80's anchor, the last one now). So the last covers
  until Review 81's anchor is written, and not after it, whatever its date.
- docs/progress/REVIEW_WAIVER.md: a dated paragraph under the grammar says so, with the optional form of a line.
- tests/test_review_waiver_names_its_anchor.py: two windows of one day told apart (the date rule alone covers; the
  anchor does not; the twin, the window it was granted in, covers); a line that names its anchor; the date rule where no
  anchor is known; each waiver on record read with an anchor that REVIEWS.md wrote.

BEFORE: on the gate as it stood, the planted waiver of the same day covers the next window (the first assertion pair).
Run: the new tests, B1461's and the gates' failing paths: 14 passed, and B1461's two tests that ask every gate to be
green and no waiver live fail as before, the count of landings being past 40 on this chain.

